# Rescue dumps written by the repair scripts. These hold REAL client rows —
# gbp-bleed-backup-2026-07-22 carries client names, tenant ids and GBP location
# ids — and were untracked but not ignored, which is one `git add -A` away from
# putting client data in the repo permanently. Ignored, not deleted: they are
# the backup someone took before a fix.
